  "summary": "Tracing the build's schematic against the specification, every functional connection and passive value matches the intended design: the NFC I2C lines (SDA/SCL/FD) each have a 10 k pull-up to VCC, VOUT and VCC of the NT3H2111 are tied to VCC, the antenna is coupled through the parallel tuning cap whose value is left as '??' (a property the spec documents, not an anomaly); the SSD1306 is strapped for I2C (D0=SCL, D1/D2 tied=SDA, CS#/D/C#/E/RD#/R/W# tied low, RES# pulled up), with the 390 k IREF, 1 u charge-pump caps, 4.7 u VCOMH, 2.2 u supply cap and VBAT on VCC; the TSC block has the 1 k series resistor to BTN and the 22 n sampling cap to GND with SHLD grounded; and the MCU reset has its 10 k pull-up plus the Tag-Connect SWD line. The only differences from the spec text are reference-designator renumbering (U3->U1, U4->U3, J1->J2, A1->A2, A2->A3, R1/R2/R3->R10/R4/R12, etc.) and hierarchical labels being shown as auto-generated NET00xx names; these are naming/ordering artifacts that do not change board behaviour, and the GPIO assignments (SWDIO=PA13, SWCLK=PA14, SWO=PB3, TSC electrode=PB5, TSC sampling=PB7, NFC=PA6/PB8/PB9, display=PB12/PB13/PB14) are consistent with the spec. No deviation that would alter the board's operation is supported by the drawing."
}

